{
    "background_story": "Damir was a humble priest in ancient Mesopotamia, devoted to the worship of Ningishzida, the serpent god of fertility and prosperity. According to legend, Ningishzida had the power to bring forth life-giving waters and ensure bountiful harvests. Damir spent years studying the ancient rituals and prayers, seeking to understand the mysteries of the serpent god. As he delved deeper into his studies, he began to experience vivid visions and dreams, which he believed were messages from Ningishzida himself. The people of his village began to notice a change in their fortunes, as the crops grew stronger and the rivers flowed with renewed vigor. They attributed their good fortune to Damir's devotion to Ningishzida, and soon he was revered as a wise and powerful intermediary between the mortal world and the realm of the gods.",
